   1405  f875
   1406  f875							; ==============================================================================
   1407  f875							; Raft (enemy type 7) — the moving, rideable platform. plans/raft_moving_plan.md
   1408  f875							; ==============================================================================
   1409  f875							; Entrance: bank0 UEDispatch -> CallPad_RaftBody (sta $1FF5 / jmp $F822) -> here;
   1410  f875							; exit: jmp ReturnPad ($FBF8, bank1's twin) -> bank0's jmp UE_Next.
   1411  f875							; CallPad rules honoured: no nested CallPad, no bank0 jsr, ZP is shared RAM.
   1412  f875							; ZP ALIAS WARNING: this code uses bank0's Temp at $88 (free here — every other
   1413  f875							; overscan Temp consumer, the joystick read and the hot-bump flag, ran before
   1414  f875							; UpdateEnemies). It must NEVER touch bank1's Temp symbol ($AD = bank0's
   1415  f875							; TickCounter — writing that would stall the game timer).
   1416  f875							;
   1417  f875							; User spec 2026-10-18: floats only on water; carries the player across and
   1418  f875							; returns; ~1.5x the player's 1 px/frame; inertia when it starts.
   1419  f875							;   Y	     = the water surface, NOT the authored y and NOT a constant: the
   1420  f875							;	       surface line drifts 0-3 lines with the TIDE (VBL stages 36+off
   1421  f875							;	       into CollisionX, kernel draws the strip as the band's last
   1422  f875							;	       (12-off) lines), so the raft is placed at 125+off and its bottom
   1423  f875							;	       row sits exactly on the moving surface — it rides the wave the
   1424  f875							;	       water does. The rider's pin (top-22 = 103+off, worst case 106)
   1425  f875							;	       stays clear of the 125 water-kill line at every tide phase.
   1426  f875							;	       This write lands after RefreshEnemyY, so the VBL draws it.
   1427  f875							;   Speed   = 1 px on even frames, 2 px on odd (EnemyRamP parity) = 1.5 px/frame.
   1428  f875							;   Inertia = a real spin-up ramp: 1 px/frame for ~30 frames (~0.5 s) then the
   1429  f875							;	       full 1/2 parity (1.5 avg), so the take-off is heavy. The state
   1430  f875							;	       lives in PlayerBombs' ($F0) spare high bits (b7 = ridden flag,
   1431  f875							;	       b6-b3 = level) — the ZP map has no free byte and the bomb count
   1432  f875							;	       keeps b2-0 (see the kernel EQU contract). Stepping off clears the
   1433  f875							;	       flag+level, so the empty raft runs at full speed and the next
   1434  f875							;	       take-off ramps again. It also holds the frame it turns around on.
   1435  f875							;   Range   = derived from the playfield, no data and no ZP: the model row-2
   1436  f875							;	       cell just beyond the raft's leading edge is read from the PF row-2
   1437  f875							;	       buffers and a SOLID cell turns it around, so the raft patrols
   1438  f875							;	       exactly the open water span of the room.
   1439  f875							;   Ride    = the raft is a FERRY: it moves ONLY while the player's box overlaps
   1440  f875							;	       its upper rows; step off and it parks immediately (the ramp state
   1441  f875							;	       is cleared too, so the next take-off ramps again). While over it a
   1442  f875							;	       non-rising player (vyHi >= 0) is pinned to the raft's top with vy
   1443  f875							;	       zeroed (gravity must never accumulate into the water) and carried
   1444  f875							;	       by the raft's step; thrust up skips the pin but keeps the carry, so
   1445  f875							;	       flying off is always possible. Leaving and re-entering the ROOM
   1446  f875							;	       resets the raft to its authored spawn x (LoadEnemyRam re-copies
   1447  f875							;	       it), which is the "reset" the user asked for.
   1448  f875							; In: X = enemy slot. Clobbers A/Y and bank0 Temp ($88).
   1449  f875							; ==============================================================================
   1450  f875							; RaftCellSolid — is the model row-2 (water row) playfield cell in display
   1451  f875							; column A solid? Reflect mapping: CTRLPF $35 (reflect) is the cave default and
   1452  f875							; a raft room has no door/bar band to switch it off. IN: A = display col 0..39.
   1453  f875							; OUT: Z=1 open (water) / Z=0 solid. Clobbers A/Y.
   1454  f875							;   cols 0-3	-> PF0 row 2 ($C5), bit 4+col (PF0 bit 4 = leftmost pixel)
   1455  f875							;   cols 4-11	-> PF1 row 2 ($C8), bit 7-(col-4)
   1456  f875							;   cols 12-19 -> PF2 row 2 ($CB), bit col-12
   1457  f875							;   cols 20-39 -> the mirrored half: source = 39-col
   1458  f875				   RaftCellSolid
   1459  f875		       c9 14		      cmp	#20
   1460  f877		       90 05		      bcc	.RCSrc
   1461  f879		       49 ff		      eor	#$ff
   1462  f87b		       18		      clc
   1463  f87c		       69 28		      adc	#40
   1464  f87e				   .RCSrc
   1465  f87e		       a8		      tay
   1466  f87f		       b9 97 f8 	      lda	RaftCellMasks,Y
   1467  f882		       c0 04		      cpy	#4
   1468  f884		       b0 03		      bcs	.RCPF1
   1469  f886		       25 c5		      and	$C5
   1470  f888		       60		      rts
   1471  f889				   .RCPF1
   1472  f889		       c0 0c		      cpy	#12
   1473  f88b		       b0 03		      bcs	.RCPF2
   1474  f88d		       25 c8		      and	$C8
   1475  f88f		       60		      rts
   1476  f890				   .RCPF2
   1477  f890		       25 cb		      and	$CB
   1478  f892		       60		      rts
