   1799  fabb							; (PairGone RETIRED, plan 5.1b 2026-10-20: the cell punch guards a repeat
   1800  fabb							;  blast on the PF buffer itself — the punched cell pair is empty, so a
   1801  fabb							;  second blast in the same room cannot score again. No rect idx4, no mask.)
   1802  fabb
   1803  fabb							; ========================================================================
   1804  fabb							; BombMarkWalls (S5.2, moved from bank0) — pinned at $FB10.
   1805  fabb							;   On the bomb 1->2 edge: punch the THIN walls in the blast window and
   1806  fabb							;   report how many were newly broken (A, caller scores +75 each).
   1807  fabb							;   Bomb left-half col +-2, clamped 0..19. Score is NOT done here — pads
   1808  fabb							;   cannot nest (ReturnPad switches to bank0), so the bank0 caller adds
   1809  fabb							;   +75 per wall.
   1810  fabb							;   Plan 5.1b (2026-10-20): the punch is CELL-based — no rect cache. The
   1811  fabb							;   PF buffers ARE the map (export: convert_room.pf_values; holes included),
   1812  fabb							;   so a bombable wall is found the same way find_rectangles finds a w==2
   1813  fabb							;   rect: a thin wall is ONE D7 logical cell = 2 display cols = a solid
   1814  fabb							;   PF bit-PAIR whose left and right neighbouring cells are empty. The
   1815  fabb							;   emitted cells are pair-aligned (both bits of a cell are always written
   1816  fabb							;   together: pf_values, ClearPFColumn, PhMaskTab), so ONE solidity read
   1817  fabb							;   per cell covers both cols, and vertical extent needs no data: each row
   1818  fabb							;   is tested on its own (the old rect h is exactly the run of thin rows —
   1819  fabb							;   find_rectangles stops a w==1 rect at a row that joins a wider run, and
   1820  fabb							;   so does the neighbour test). Col 0 (screen border, and its mirror col
   1821  fabb							;   39) is never destroyable — the old `rect.x == 0` skip.
   1822  fabb							;   Double-score guard = the buffer: the punched pair is empty, so a second
   1823  fabb							;   blast in the same room finds no cell (the old WallMask bits and PairGone
   1824  fabb							;   are gone; walls return on re-entry, D1-B). WallMask (BombPacked b3-6) is
   1825  fabb							;   retired: HotOverlapBody now tests its parent hot cell's PF bit.
   1826  fabb							;   Cost: ≤4 cells × 3 rows × ~3 cell probes; blast edge only.
   1827  fabb							; ========================================================================
   1828  fabb							; AddScoreCarry — the rare path of AddScore (>= 100 points carried out of ScoreTe).
   1829  fabb							; Entered with D=1 and C=1. Ripples the carry through ScoreHu and ScoreTh; a
   1830  fabb							; carry INTO ScoreTh is a 10,000-point crossing, and ScoreTh's low digit
   1831  fabb							; (ten-thousands) is then 0 or 5 exactly on a 50,000 / 100,000 mark — that is
   1832  fabb							; the EXTRA LIFE (user 2026-10-27: every 50,000, max MAX_LIVES = 8). A carry out
   1833  fabb							; of ScoreTh means 999,999 + more: the score sticks at 999,999. Runs once per
   1834  fabb							; 100 points at most, and each 10,000 crossing happens once, so no life can be
   1835  fabb							; awarded twice for the same mark. Tested by tools/test_addscore.py.
   1836  fabb				   AddScoreCarry
   1837  fabb		       a5 f4		      lda	ScoreHu
   1838  fabd		       69 00		      adc	#0	; + the carry (BCD)
   1839  fabf		       85 f4		      sta	ScoreHu
   1840  fac1		       90 18		      bcc	.ASCdone	; no 10,000 crossing
   1841  fac3		       a5 f3		      lda	ScoreTh
   1842  fac5		       69 00		      adc	#0	; + the carry (BCD)
   1843  fac7		       b0 16		      bcs	.ASCcap	; past 999,999
   1844  fac9		       85 f3		      sta	ScoreTh
   1845  facb		       29 0f		      and	#$0F	; ten-thousands digit
   1846  facd		       f0 04		      beq	.ASClife	; x0,000 : 100,000 / 200,000 ...
   1847  facf		       c9 05		      cmp	#5
   1848  fad1		       d0 08		      bne	.ASCdone	; only x5,000... i.e. 50,000 / 150,000 ...
   1849  fad3				   .ASClife
   1850  fad3		       a5 ac		      lda	PlayerLives
   1851  fad5		       c9 08		      cmp	#MAX_LIVES
   1852  fad7		       b0 02		      bcs	.ASCdone
   1853  fad9		       e6 ac		      inc	PlayerLives
   1854  fadb				   .ASCdone
   1855  fadb		       d8		      cld
   1856  fadc		       4c f8 fb 	      jmp	ReturnPad
   1857  fadf				   .ASCcap
   1858  fadf		       a9 99		      lda	#$99
   1859  fae1		       85 f3		      sta	ScoreTh
   1860  fae3		       85 f4		      sta	ScoreHu
   1861  fae5		       85 f5		      sta	ScoreTe
   1862  fae7		       d0 f2		      bne	.ASCdone	; A = $99, always taken
