   2347  fe03							; water line is what the raft floats on
   2348  fe03
   2349  fe03							; --- does the player count as "over the raft"? --------------------------
   2350  fe03							; The raft is a FERRY (user rule 2026-10-18): it moves ONLY while he is over
   2351  fe03							; it, parks the moment he steps off, and its position resets on room entry
   2352  fe03							; (LoadEnemyRam re-copies the record's spawn x). Gating the whole motion
   2353  fe03							; block here is what makes it park; the pin/carry later still applies while
   2354  fe03							; riding. The test runs against the CURRENT x (before the step), i.e. the
   2355  fe03							; raft he is actually standing on.
   2356  fe03		       a5 80		      lda	RoomX
   2357  fe05		       38		      sec
   2358  fe06		       f5 bd		      sbc	EnemyRamX,X
   2359  fe08		       18		      clc
   2360  fe09		       69 06		      adc	#RAFTER_XOFF
   2361  fe0b		       c9 0e		      cmp	#RAFTER_XSPAN
   2362  fe0d		       b0 13		      bcs	.RaftNoRide	; no X overlap: nobody aboard
   2363  fe0f		       a5 81		      lda	RoomY
   2364  fe11		       38		      sec
   2365  fe12		       f5 e2		      sbc	EnemyRamY,X
   2366  fe14		       18		      clc
   2367  fe15		       69 16		      adc	#RAFTER_PINFIT
   2368  fe17		       c9 1c		      cmp	#RAFTER_YSPAN
   2369  fe19		       b0 07		      bcs	.RaftNoRide	; not in the raft's upper rows
   2370  fe1b		       a5 94		      lda	vyHi
   2371  fe1d		       30 03		      bmi	.RaftNoRide	; rising: let him fly away (no pin)
   2372  fe1f		       4c 2b fe 	      jmp	.RaftGo
   2373  fe22				   .RaftNoRide
   2374  fe22							; nobody over the raft: PARK it (no motion) and clear the ramp state so the
   2375  fe22							; next take-off ramps again; the bomb count in b2-0 is preserved
   2376  fe22		       a5 f0		      lda	$F0
   2377  fe24		       29 07		      and	#%00000111
   2378  fe26		       85 f0		      sta	$F0
   2379  fe28		       4c f8 fb 	      jmp	ReturnPad
   2380  fe2b				   .RaftGo
   2381  fe2b							; --- pin FIRST: the rider stays on the raft even on a TURN frame --------
   2382  fe2b							; A raft boxed in by solid row-2 cells (or parked against a rail) turns
   2383  fe2b							; every frame and never moves; the turn path returns before the carry, so
   2384  fe2b							; pinning here is what keeps a rider standing on it. Without it he fell
   2385  fe2b							; through a stuck raft into the water kill line and respawned forever
   2386  fe2b							; (user report 2026-10-22: "player position keeps changing, zig-zags").
   2387  fe2b							; The vyHi < 0 escape is the gate's `.RaftNoRide` (rising is not a ride).
   2388  fe2b		       b5 e2		      lda	EnemyRamY,X
   2389  fe2d		       38		      sec
   2390  fe2e		       e9 16		      sbc	#RAFTER_PINFIT
   2391  fe30		       85 81		      sta	RoomY	; feet on the raft's top
   2392  fe32		       a9 00		      lda	#0
   2393  fe34		       85 93		      sta	vyLo
   2394  fe36		       85 94		      sta	vyHi	; landing kills the accumulated fall speed
   2395  fe38							; --- take-off ramp (inertia): heaviest right after boarding -------------
   2396  fe38							; State = PlayerBombs' ($F0) spare HIGH bits: b7 = "ridden last frame",
   2397  fe38							; b6-b3 = the ramp level (0-15); b2-0 stay the bomb count. Adding $10 never
   2398  fe38							; carries into b2-0, and the drop's `dec` is guarded by a non-zero count so
   2399  fe38							; it cannot borrow upward either (see the kernel EQU for the contract).
   2400  fe38							; Riding advances the level every 2nd frame: the raft leaves at 1 px/frame
   2401  fe38							; and reaches the full 1/2 parity (1.5 avg) after ~30 frames (~0.5 s), the
   2402  fe38							; heavy take-off. Empty (b7 clear) or level 15: full speed straight away.
   2403  fe38		       a5 f0		      lda	$F0
   2404  fe3a		       10 08		      bpl	.RaftAtSpeed	; b7 clear = nobody aboard -> no ramp
   2405  fe3c		       c9 f8		      cmp	#%11111000	; flag + all four level bits = spun up
   2406  fe3e		       f0 04		      beq	.RaftAtSpeed
   2407  fe40		       a9 01		      lda	#1	; still ramping: 1 px/frame
   2408  fe42		       d0 07		      bne	.RaftHaveStep	; always
   2409  fe44				   .RaftAtSpeed
   2410  fe44		       a5 c2		      lda	EnemyRamP
   2411  fe46		       29 01		      and	#1
   2412  fe48		       18		      clc
   2413  fe49		       69 01		      adc	#1	; 1 px even frames, 2 px odd = 1.5 px/frame
